{% set local_problem %}
<p>New Hope's humid climate is hard on exposed wood. When gutters leak or overflow, water runs behind them and soaks into fascia boards. Over time, that moisture causes rot that can spread to rafters and roof structure if not addressed.</p>

<p>Many New Hope homes have some fascia damage — especially older properties where original gutters have been leaking for years. Sometimes it's obvious; sometimes it's hidden under paint.</p>

<p>Installing new gutters on rotted fascia doesn't make sense. The gutters won't stay attached properly, and the underlying damage continues. We fix the foundation first, then install gutters that will last.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>We start with careful inspection, checking fascia and soffit for water damage, soft spots, and rot. We'll show you what we find.</p>

<p>For damaged areas, we remove existing gutters, cut out rotted wood, and install new fascia. We use quality materials appropriate for your home's age and style.</p>

<p>Then we install new gutters on the solid foundation — properly attached and designed to prevent the overflow that caused damage in the first place.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've been repairing fascia and installing gutters in eastern Madison County for over 20 years. We handle both jobs, which means better coordination and a single warranty covering everything.</p>

<p>Our crews do quality carpentry work. When we're done, your roof edge is completely protected from fascia to downspout.</p>
{% endset %}
